#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# appell_f4

#% text
# `appell_f4(a, b, c1, c2, x, y)` gives the Appell hypergeometric function `F4` of two variables.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `F4 = sum (a)_(m+n) (b)_(m+n)/((c1)_m (c2)_n m! n!) x^m y^n` for `sqrt(|x|) + sqrt(|y|) < 1` (DLMF 16.13.4).

#% item
# Numerical values: the sum over the rows of one variable of Gauss functions `hypergeometric_2f1` in the other (DLMF 16.13 summed over one index), the variable of smaller modulus outside; the inner Gauss function continues beyond the unit disk. Values are given where the row sum converges.

#% item
# At `x = 0` or `y = 0` the function is a Gauss function.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
appell_f4(3, 2, 1, 2, 1/5, 0.1)
#% output
#= 8.826000820593443

#% cell
appell_f4(-2, -1, -2.3, 2/3 + im, 0.1, 0.3)
#% output
#= 1.1899665551839465 - 0.41538461538461535im

#% cell
n(appell_f4(3, 2, 1, 2, 1/5, 1/7), 20)
#% output
#= 15.54380683207932956859

#% cell
appell_f4(a, b, c1, c2, 0, y)
#% output
#= hypergeometric_2f1(a, b, c2, y)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `appell_f1`, `appell_f2`, `appell_f3`
